config BR2_PACKAGE_DEVMAPPER_UDEV
	bool "devmapper-udev (libdevmapper with udev synchronisation)"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_LVM2
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HAS_UDEV
	help
	  lvm2's device-mapper library built a second time, after
	  systemd, with --enable-udev_sync, replacing the copy the lvm2
	  package installs. Buildroot cannot build lvm2 itself that way:
	  systemd (homed) needs cryptsetup, cryptsetup needs lvm2, so
	  lvm2 is built before libudev exists.

	  Without the synchronisation libdevmapper makes and removes the
	  /dev/mapper nodes itself. systemd-homed opens a home and at
	  once marks its DM device for deferred removal (it goes when the
	  home is unmounted), and libdevmapper removes the node right
	  then while the device lives on; udev's symlink had failed
	  against that node. An active home then has no /dev/mapper
	  node, and every homework run on it -- the lock screen's and
	  sudo's password check, a password change, the rebalance every
	  few minutes -- fails with "Home mount incompletely set up".
	  With the synchronisation libdevmapper leaves the nodes to
	  udev, as every distribution does.
